{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added a per-feed `refresh_interval` (integer minutes, 0 = use the global interval). The build and existing unit and integration tests pass; the new behaviour itself has no tests of its own.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **Migration**: new `feeds.refresh_interval int not null default 0` column.\n- **API**: the field is in the feed object and accepted by `PUT /v1/feeds/{feedID}`; values below 0 or above 525600 (one year) are rejected with a validation error. The Go client models carry it too.\n- **Web UI**: the feed edit form has a number input named `refresh_interval`; an empty value is treated as 0 and non-numeric input is rejected.\n- **Scheduler**: `ScheduleNextCheck` uses the per-feed interval when it is above 0, instead of the round-robin or entry-frequency calculation.\n\nBehaviours you might not assume:\n- A server-requested delay (Retry-After, TTL, Cache-Control) longer than the feed's interval still wins, capped at the scheduler's max interval.\n- A per-feed interval is not capped by the global max interval, so a feed can be polled less often than the global maximum.\n- Changing the interval to a non-zero value pulls `next_check_at` forward if it was further away than the new interval, so a shorter interval takes effect without waiting out the old schedule.\n- The field is not accepted on feed creation or carried in OPML import/export; it can only be set by editing a feed.\n\nThe two new translation keys (form label and validation error) are in all 24 locale files, but only French is translated; the rest use the English text.", "t": 1794463471.829}
{"tool": "_result", "name": "finish", "chars": 55, "t": 1794463471.829}
